---
title: Chimichurri Quinoa Salad
course: side
cuisine: argentine
servings: 2
time_active: 15
time_total: 25
leftovers: good
tags: [make-ahead]
pairs: [argentine-beef-tenderloin-with-malbec-sauce]
---

Rinse @quinoa{1/2%cup} and combine with @water{1%cup}(or low-sodium vegetable broth) in a #small saucepan{}. Bring to a boil, then cover and simmer until the liquid is absorbed, ~{12-15%minutes}. Fluff with a fork and spread on a plate to cool.

Whisk @fresh parsley{2%tbsp}(finely chopped), @red wine vinegar{1%tbsp}, @olive oil{2%tbsp}, @dried oregano{1/2%tsp}, @?red pepper flakes{1%pinch}, and a pinch each of @salt and @black pepper{}.

Just before serving, toss @baby arugula{2%cups} and the cooled quinoa with the vinaigrette.

> The quinoa and vinaigrette keep a day in the fridge, stored separately. Rewarm the quinoa slightly before tossing.
